-- title:
--   Reducedness of the level-zero quotient of the edge chart ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal O$, and assume that the principal ideal $(\pi) = \mathrm{span}\{\pi\}$ is maximal in $\mathcal O$; let $r$ be a natural number. Form the edge ring $B =$ `edgeQuot 𝒪 π`, the quotient of the polynomial ring $\mathcal O[X_0,X_1]$ in two variables (indexed by `Fin 2`) by the principal ideal generated by `edgeRel 𝒪 π`, and then the chart ring $A =$ `chartERing 𝒪 π r`, defined as the localisation of $B$ away from the element `edgeQuot.discr 𝒪 π r`, i.e. the image in $B$ of `edgeDiscr 𝒪 r`. The theorem asserts that the quotient of $A$ by the ideal generated by $(\,\iota(\pi)\,)^{0+1}$, where $\iota : \mathcal O \to A$ is the structure morphism, is a reduced ring: every nilpotent element of $A/\iota(\pi)A$ vanishes. The exponent is written $0+1$, so this is the level-zero member of the family of quotients by powers $\iota(\pi)^{n+1}$; no hypothesis is imposed on $r$.
--
--   This is the statement that the special fibre of the standard edge chart in the Mumford-type construction underlying the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation is reduced, the chart-level form of the assertion that the node $\xi\eta = 0$ is a reduced curve. It is used for the reducedness of the special level of the glue datum (`MumfordGlue.specialLevel_isField_isReduced_dim_infinite`) and in `finiteType_and_isReduced_tensorProduct_chartERing_of_isAlgClosed`.
